  "evidence": "TEXT_E: Authority—maintain defence spending at ≥2% of GDP with annual real-terms rises; retain the nuclear deterrent; create a national infrastructure police force; merge SFO into NCA; expand cyber security; build 10,000 prison places and toughen community sentences; impose minimum rail service levels during strikes; stronger online safety rules; reduce net migration and tighten family/student visas. Loyalty—reject a new Scottish independence referendum; protect Gibraltar; veterans’ Board and NI holiday; United Kingdom Shared Prosperity Fund to bind the Union; withdraw from London Fisheries Convention and establish a UK regime. Care—NHS real-terms increase of at least £8bn; expand mental health workforce; faster cancer diagnosis; carers’ leave; social care funding reforms. Equality—strengthen gig‑economy protections; protect Pupil Premium; free primary breakfasts; technical education, apprenticeships, and retraining. Proportionality—balance the budget by the mid‑2020s; means‑test Winter Fuel Payments; include home value in care means tests; crack down on tax evasion/avoidance; binding shareholder votes on executive pay and publish pay ratios; raise the National Living Wage to 60% of median. Sanctity—25‑year environment plan, anti‑litter and air‑quality measures; CCTV in slaughterhouses (while supporting shale development). TEXT_D: Authority—defence at 2% with reduced nuclear posture; +£300m/year for policing; retain HRA/ECHR; roll back bulk powers; replace Prevent; presumption against short sentences; votes at 16; STV and wider constitutional reforms. Loyalty—second EU referendum with option to remain; seek close EU ties (single market/customs access); liberal immigration and large asylum resettlement pledges; constitutional federalism. Care—1p Income Tax rise ringfenced for NHS and social care; mental health parity with national waiting times; uprate working‑age benefits; scrap two‑child limit and bedroom tax; childcare expansion; extensive renters’ protections; 50,000 resettlement places and 3,000 unaccompanied children. Equality—employee participation/ownership; ban letting fees and cap deposits; longer tenancies; inclusive SRE; remove students from migration stats; cap donations and strengthen lobbying rules. Proportionality—eliminate day‑to‑day deficit by 2020; dedicated health/care tax and independent watchdog; strengthen anti‑avoidance; review business rates; start‑up allowance. Sanctity—strong green agenda (zero‑carbon homes, 60% renewables by 2030, diesel ban by 2025, zero‑waste); oppose fracking; regulate cannabis for adults.",
  "reasoning": "Because authority and loyalty are the electorate’s top priorities, TEXT_E aligns better by emphasizing defence and nuclear deterrence, tougher sentencing and policing, immigration reduction, minimum service during strikes, and explicit unionism (rejecting a new Scottish referendum and protecting Gibraltar). While TEXT_D scores highly on care and equality, its liberal stances on surveillance, sentencing, drugs, EU alignment, and immigration make it less aligned with the profile’s strongest (authority/loyalty) foundations.",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "winner": "TEXT_E"
}
